export anchor PatchworkQuiltStyle:
    number: 107
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Patchwork quilt
    idea: The dashboard is one bound quilt, its blocks butted edge to edge in homey fabrics, each with a muslin centre that holds a number, a project or the chart.
    base: light
    palette:
        calico: #f6efe2, the page behind the quilt
        muslin: #fffaf0, block centres, the nav and the header strip
        denim: #2f4f7a, the quilt binding, section strips, progress patches and the focus ring
        barnRed: #9b2f2a, the brand label, the primary button, Behind and overdue
        butter: #f2d58a, the stripe fabric, the bell and the current tab
        sage: #8fae8b, half square triangles and the sprig fabric
        fern: #1f5a33, the On track tag
        toffee: #7a4a00, the At risk tag
        ink: #2b2622, text and block edges
        thread: #5a5048, meta and times
    type:
        Two stacks. Headings and numbers use Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Zilla
        Slab, Georgia in bold. Text uses Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI,
        system-ui. The greeting is 38px at 1.1, numbers 52px, block titles
        19px, section strips 22px, body 16px at 1.5, meta 14px.
    layout:
        The header is a muslin strip framed in denim with a barn red label
        block holding a pieced square logo and Brightwork, then the search,
        New project, a butter bell and a triangle pieced MO avatar. Under it
        the nav is six equal muslin cells split by dashed quilting lines,
        the current cell filled with butter stripe and the word in a small
        boxed label. The quilt has a 12px denim binding with a dashed stitch
        inside and four columns of blocks with no gaps. A wide medallion
        block framed in red half square triangles holds Welcome home, Mara,
        the date and a red outlined 4 tasks are overdue with an octagon.
        Four log cabin blocks in blue gingham, butter stripe, red gingham
        and sprig hold the numbers in muslin centres. A denim strip titles
        Projects, then six blocks three across, each a fabric frame around
        a muslin centre with name, meta, ten little denim patches for
        progress, the percent and a dashed status tag. The last row pairs a
        gingham chart block, where 14 dashed day columns hold butter stripe
        or denim dot bars, with a sprig block for News from the sewing
        circle. Below 980px the quilt is two columns, below 640px one.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Fabric frames are 16 to 20px wide around each muslin centre.
    density: Medium. Blocks touch with no gaps, like a finished quilt top.
    corners: Square, 2px at most on controls.
    borders: A 12px denim binding with a dashed stitch inside, 2px ink edges on centres and 1.5px dashed quilting lines.
    shadows: None. Texture comes from fabric patterns made with gradients, gingham, dots, stripe, half square triangles and sprig.
    icons:
        Solid shapes with white marks at 16px. A ticked circle for On
        track, a triangle for At risk, a square with a down arrow for
        Behind and an octagon for overdue, inside a dashed tag with the word.
    focus: A 3px denim outline offset 3px, a 6px muslin gap and a 3px barn red ring outside.
    tone: Homey and kind, such as Welcome home and News from the sewing circle.
